    {
      "id": "claim_9f88fc7c21de4f0ca988583e7f1b201c",
      "statement": "Every celld command obeys three enforced rules — stdout carries data and stderr carries prose, listings are bounded by default and state what they withheld plus how to continue, and a closed pipe is a successful stop — and the Record/Resumable trait pair makes --json and a resume cursor impossible to half-implement.",
