    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c0062b8fc8844fb683e523c938f9c949",
      "statement": "The reachable-node set is a list of equal entrances rather than a route (any live node forwards to the owner), each request is signed per entrance because the signature binds the target node, and per-subject source labels and timeouts (migration-shaped, not probe-shaped) travel with the operation.",
      "evidence": [
